<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan awards Feb fuel oil sell tender at $101/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan awards Feb fuel oil sell tender at $101/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp has awarded its tender to sell February high sulphur fuel oil at $101 per tonne, $20 off from its award for January deliveries, a company source said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>CPC sold the 30,000 tonnes of 3-percent sulphur grade fuel oil cargo lifting February 18-27 from Koahsiung to a &quot;trader&quot;, the source said.</p>
<p>CPC last sold two 30,000-tonne cargoes lifting January 11-30 at $121-$122 to a Singapore trader.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
